    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d920">

                <pb facs="1083" n="987" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg987"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1087.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: The Department is informed that the
                    Home Mission Board of the Southern Baptist Convention, an incorporated
                    organization, owns a considerable amount of real and personal property in Habana
                    and in San Miguel, Cuba. All this property was lately in charge of Dr. Ed.
                    Belot, who was assisted in the care of it by his niece, Miss Joerg, Prado 67,
                    Habana. Upon a recent report of Dr. Belot’s death, the Home Mission Board cabled
                    Miss Joerg, authorizing her to take charge of the property in question, and it
                    is desired that the British consul at Habana may be informed of the fact, in
                    order that he may render her such good offices as may be needful and proper.</p>
                <p>The Department will be greatly obliged if your excellency will be so good as to
                    telegraph to this effect to Her Majesty’s consular representative at Habana.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
